qmodem_sipd: the dialog is closed on both sides

send_dialog_bye() built the BYE only from the registered (outbound) INVITE, so two
teardowns were missing.  A call the cellular side originated had no dialog record to
build a BYE from: when the cellular leg hung up, the consumer detached its media but
sent nothing to the LAN, and the LAN phone stayed connected with a running timer.  A
call the LAN originated left the consumer as the UAS of the dialog, which builds its
BYE with its own tag on the From and the peer's tag on the To (RFC 3261 15.1.2), and
no such request was ever formed.

Remember the INVITE that opened the dialog by holding a second reference to it, take
the peer's Contact, the peer's From, the local AOR and the tag placed on the 200
while that response is still being built, and send the BYE as UAC or as UAS according
to which side opened the dialog.  A BYE inside an established dialog proves itself by that
identity (RFC 3261 12.2.2): answering it with 401 leaves the call up, because a
common UA does not re-authenticate an in-dialog request, so the identity check now
runs first and a matched dialog is not challenged.

